# Frontend.
#
# Deliberately empty. The app reads no VITE_ variable: the API base path is the constant /api/v1 in
# the shared package, because the browser talks to the same origin that served the page. There is
# no address to configure.
#
# The gateway's one runtime setting lives on the container, not here:
#
#   BACKEND_ORIGIN   Where nginx proxies /api/*. Inside a single Compose stack the default
#                    http://backend:3000 is correct. A deployment that runs the API as a separate
#                    Coolify resource sets this to that resource's internal address.
#
# If a public value is ever needed in the browser, it goes here with a VITE_ prefix and nowhere
# else. Everything with that prefix is compiled into code every visitor downloads, so a credential
# placed here is a published credential. `npm run test` reads the built bundle and fails if a
# backend variable name or a connection string appears in it.
